   "created_at": "2026-01-22T07:25:39Z",
   "updated_at": "2026-01-22T07:25:39Z",
   "body": "> dirty invokes setDirty on every keystroke\n\nReact bails out if it's the same value `onChange`, so it doesn't cause a re-render until the input value returns to the initial value. So for an initially empty input, `filled`/`dirty` change together (batched re-render) and no extra re-renders occur while typing afterwards until the input is cleared again\n\nWith #3820, a re-render occurs once when focusing the control (`focused` state), and then again once on the first keystroke, but not any point after that, for an initially empty input",
   "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
   "pin": null,
